This study presents the University of Modena's contribution to the 7th International Competition on Offline Handwriting Text Recognition, where the key challenge was the date recognition task. Our solution, DARE, involves a two-stage approach. First, the date zone is localized within the handwritten word image. Then, the date string is recognized using a combination of a connectionist out-of-vocabulary (OOV) model and a character-level deep neural network. Our connectionist model leverages a deep neural network to extract features from the handwriting image, while the character-level model is a convolutional neural network that predicts the character sequence. Our system achieved a 0.69 error rate on the DASH2015 test dataset, ranking second in the competition. Furthermore, we discuss the design choices and the training methodology behind our successful submission. Our code and pre-trained models are publicly available at https://github.com/ultrafunkteam/dare. 

